{%- liquid
  # The dusk-range campaign pair ships with the theme as immutable webp
  # assets; an image picker still lets a reviewed release swap the art.
  assign hero_image_label = 'homepage.hero.image_label' | t
  assign hero_image = section.settings.image
  assign hero_mobile_image = section.settings.mobile_image
  assign hero_image_alt = hero_image_label
-%}

<section id="home-hero" class="sl-hero" aria-labelledby="HeroTitle-{{ section.id }}">
  <figure class="sl-hero__backdrop{% if section.settings.video == blank %} sl-hero__backdrop--motion{% endif %}">
    {%- if section.settings.video != blank -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        A muted autoplaying loop. The photo below remains the fallback for
        installs without a clip — and the LCP either way, since video_tag
        ships its own poster frame.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {{ section.settings.video | video_tag: autoplay: true, loop: true, muted: true, controls: false, playsinline: true, class: 'sl-hero__video', image_size: '1672x' }}
    {%- elsif hero_image -%}
      <picture>
        {%- if hero_mobile_image -%}
          <source
            media="(max-width: 749px)"
            srcset="{{ hero_mobile_image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ hero_mobile_image | image_url: width: 750 }} 750w, {{ hero_mobile_image | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w, {{ hero_mobile_image | image_url: width: 1122 }} 1122w"
            sizes="100vw">
        {%- endif -%}
        {{ hero_image | image_url: width: 1672 | image_tag:
          class: 'sl-hero__image',
          widths: '750, 1100, 1400, 1672',
          sizes: '100vw',
          loading: 'eager',
          fetchpriority: 'high',
          alt: hero_image_alt }}
      </picture>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Theme webps are served whole via asset_url: the legacy sizing
        filter does not process webp and emits the no-image placeholder.
        Both files ship pre-optimized under ~110 KB.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <picture>
        <source
          media="(max-width: 749px)"
          srcset="{{ 'caddieinsight-range-hero-mobile.webp' | asset_url }}">
        <img
          class="sl-hero__image"
          src="{{ 'caddieinsight-range-hero-desktop.webp' | asset_url }}"
          width="1672"
          height="941"
          alt="{{ hero_image_alt | escape }}"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          decoding="async">
      </picture>
    {%- endif -%}
  </figure>

  {%- comment -%}
    Shot tracers. The broadcast-golf visual, generated live: glowing ball
    flights arc from the golfer's corner of the photograph into the dusk
    sky every few seconds. Pure canvas, zero media bytes, and the script
    refuses to run under prefers-reduced-motion or Save-Data, parks
    itself offscreen via IntersectionObserver, and stops in hidden tabs
    (rAF). The hero remains complete without it — this layer is
    atmosphere, never content.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <canvas class="sl-hero__tracers" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

  <div class="sl-hero__inner sl-wrap">
    <div class="sl-hero__copy sl-reveal is-in">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="sl-hero__brand"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <h1 id="HeroTitle-{{ section.id }}" class="sl-hero__title">{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Bring one clear move to the range.' }}</h1>
      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <p class="sl-hero__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="sl-hero__actions">
        {%- if section.settings.primary_label != blank and section.settings.primary_url != blank -%}
          <a href="{{ section.settings.primary_url }}"
             class="sl-btn sl-hero__primary"
             data-app-primary-cta
             data-app-signed-out-label="{{ section.settings.primary_label | escape }}"
             data-app-signed-out-url="{{ section.settings.primary_url }}">
            <span data-app-cta-label>{{ section.settings.primary_label }}</span>
            <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.secondary_label != blank and section.settings.secondary_url != blank -%}
          <a href="{{ section.settings.secondary_url }}" class="sl-btn sl-hero__secondary">{{ section.settings.secondary_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if section.settings.chip1 != blank or section.settings.chip2 != blank or section.settings.chip3 != blank -%}
        <ul class="sl-hero__proof" aria-label="{{ 'homepage.hero.proof_label' | t }}">
          {%- if section.settings.chip1 != blank -%}<li>{{ section.settings.chip1 }}</li>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.chip2 != blank -%}<li>{{ section.settings.chip2 }}</li>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.chip3 != blank -%}<li>{{ section.settings.chip3 }}</li>{%- endif -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.fine_print != blank -%}
        <p class="sl-hero__fine">{{ section.settings.fine_print }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sl-hero__signal-band sl-wrap">
    <aside class="sl-hero__signal sl-reveal sl-reveal--d1 is-in" aria-label="{{ 'homepage.hero.signal_label' | t }}">
      <div class="sl-hero__signal-head">
        <span>{{ 'homepage.hero.signal_status' | t }}</span>
        <span class="sl-hero__signal-live"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ 'homepage.hero.signal_ready' | t }}</span>
      </div>
      <div class="sl-hero__trace" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'homepage.hero.trace_label' | t }}">
        {%- comment -%}
          The live read. One arc, drawn at the engine's own benchmark: the
          backswing draws for three beats, holds at the top, and the strike
          retraces it in one — the 3:1 tempo_ratio target, animated. Pose
          crosshairs blink in as landmarks resolve; the pulse is impact.
          pathLength="100" normalizes both paths so the dash keyframes are
          percentages, not measured lengths. Every default below is the
          fully drawn state, so reduced-motion (and print) get a complete
          still trace rather than an empty box.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <svg class="sl-hero__trace-svg" viewBox="0 0 280 88" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path class="sl-hero__trace-arc" d="M 54 66 C 96 46, 148 10, 214 20" pathLength="100"/>
          <path class="sl-hero__trace-strike" d="M 54 66 C 96 46, 148 10, 214 20" pathLength="100"/>
          <g class="sl-hero__trace-tick sl-hero__trace-tick--mid" transform="translate(125 32)">
            <path d="M -5 0 H 5 M 0 -5 V 5"/>
          </g>
          <g class="sl-hero__trace-tick sl-hero__trace-tick--top" transform="translate(214 20)">
            <path d="M -5 0 H 5 M 0 -5 V 5"/>
          </g>
          <circle class="sl-hero__trace-impact" cx="54" cy="66" r="14"/>
          <circle class="sl-hero__trace-ball" cx="54" cy="66" r="3.2"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <dl class="sl-hero__signal-grid">
        <div><dt>{{ 'homepage.hero.club_label' | t }}</dt><dd>{{ section.settings.signal_club }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>{{ 'homepage.hero.priority_label' | t }}</dt><dd>{{ section.settings.signal_priority }}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>{{ 'homepage.hero.target_label' | t }}</dt><dd>{{ section.settings.signal_target }}</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="sl-hero__signal-note">{{ 'homepage.hero.signal_disclosure' | t }}</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  (function () {
    'use strict';
    var reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
    var conn = navigator.connection;
    if (reduce.matches || (conn && conn.saveData)) return;
    var canvas = document.querySelector('.sl-hero__tracers');
    var hero = document.getElementById('home-hero');
    if (!canvas || !hero || !canvas.getContext) return;
    var ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
    var dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
    var width = 0, height = 0, tracers = [], raf = 0, visible = false, nextAt = 0;

    function resize() {
      width = hero.clientWidth; height = hero.clientHeight;
      canvas.width = Math.round(width * dpr);
      canvas.height = Math.round(height * dpr);
      ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
    }

    /* One flight: a quadratic arc from the golfer's corner of the photo
       into the sky. Eased fast-then-floating, drawn as a fading trail
       with a bright head — the TV shot-tracer, not confetti. */
    function spawn(now) {
      var phone = width < 750;
      var x0 = width * (phone ? 0.16 : 0.24) + Math.random() * width * 0.06;
      var y0 = height * 0.82 + Math.random() * height * 0.05;
      var x2 = width * (0.72 + Math.random() * 0.3);
      var y2 = height * (0.06 + Math.random() * 0.2);
      var x1 = (x0 + x2) * 0.44;
      var y1 = y2 - height * (0.18 + Math.random() * 0.1);
      var warm = Math.random() < 0.72;
      tracers.push({
        x0: x0, y0: y0, x1: x1, y1: y1, x2: x2, y2: y2,
        born: now, flight: 2600 + Math.random() * 700, linger: 1500,
        hue: warm ? '255, 173, 98' : '238, 242, 239'
      });
    }

    function pointAt(t, p) {
      var u = 1 - t;
      return {
        x: u * u * p.x0 + 2 * u * t * p.x1 + t * t * p.x2,
        y: u * u * p.y0 + 2 * u * t * p.y1 + t * t * p.y2
      };
    }

    function frame(now) {
      raf = 0;
      if (!visible || reduce.matches) { ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height); return; }
      ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);
      var phone = width < 750;
      if (now >= nextAt && tracers.length < (phone ? 1 : 2)) {
        spawn(now);
        nextAt = now + 3800 + Math.random() * 2700;
      }
      for (var i = tracers.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        var tr = tracers[i];
        var age = now - tr.born;
        if (age > tr.flight + tr.linger) { tracers.splice(i, 1); continue; }
        var raw = Math.min(age / tr.flight, 1);
        var head = 1 - Math.pow(1 - raw, 2.4);
        var fade = age <= tr.flight ? 1 : 1 - (age - tr.flight) / tr.linger;
        var steps = 34;
        for (var s = 1; s <= steps; s++) {
          var t1 = head * (s / steps);
          var t0 = head * ((s - 1) / steps);
          var a = pointAt(t0, tr), b = pointAt(t1, tr);
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.moveTo(a.x, a.y); ctx.lineTo(b.x, b.y);
          ctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(' + tr.hue + ',' + (0.34 * fade * Math.pow(s / steps, 2.2)).toFixed(3) + ')';
          ctx.lineWidth = phone ? 1.4 : 1.8;
          ctx.lineCap = 'round';
          ctx.stroke();
        }
        if (age <= tr.flight) {
          var hp = pointAt(head, tr);
          var glow = ctx.createRadialGradient(hp.x, hp.y, 0, hp.x, hp.y, phone ? 7 : 10);
          glow.addColorStop(0, 'rgba(255, 232, 200, ' + (0.9 * fade).toFixed(3) + ')');
          glow.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(' + tr.hue + ', 0)');
          ctx.fillStyle = glow;
          ctx.beginPath();
          ctx.arc(hp.x, hp.y, phone ? 7 : 10, 0, Math.PI * 2);
          ctx.fill();
        }
      }
      if (tracers.length || visible) raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame);
    }

    function wake() { if (!raf && visible) raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame); }
    var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
      visible = entries[0].isIntersecting && !document.hidden;
      if (visible) { resize(); wake(); }
    });
    io.observe(hero);
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () {
      visible = !document.hidden && visible;
      if (!document.hidden) { visible = true; wake(); }
    });
    window.addEventListener('resize', function () { resize(); }, { passive: true });
    reduce.addEventListener('change', function () { tracers = []; });
    resize();
  })();
</script>

{% stylesheet %}
.sl-hero__tracers {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  z-index: 3;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  pointer-events: none;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .sl-hero__tracers { display: none; }
}
.sl-hero {
  position: relative;
  isolation: isolate;
  min-height: clamp(700px, 78svh, 860px);
  overflow: hidden;
  background: var(--sl-night);
  color: var(--sl-bg);
}
.sl-hero::before,
.sl-hero::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.sl-hero::before {
  z-index: 1;
  background:
    linear-gradient(105deg, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.96) 0%, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.84) 38%, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.28) 64%, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.12) 100%),
    linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.88) 0%, transparent 42%, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.14) 100%);
}
.sl-hero::after {
  z-index: 2;
  opacity: 0.2;
  background-image:
    linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 1px, transparent 1px),
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 1px, transparent 1px);
  background-size: 64px 64px;
  -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, #000, transparent 74%);
  mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, #000, transparent 74%);
}
.sl-hero__backdrop,
.sl-hero__backdrop picture {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  margin: 0;
}
.sl-hero__image {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
  object-position: center;
}
.sl-hero__video,
.sl-hero__video video,
video.sl-hero__video {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  object-fit: cover;
}
/* With no video set, the photograph carries the motion: a slow drift,
   far side of the reduced-motion gate. Alternate keeps the loop seamless. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .sl-hero__backdrop--motion .sl-hero__image {
    animation: sl-hero-drift 28s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
    will-change: transform;
  }
  /* Load choreography: the copy stack rises line by line, once. */
  .sl-hero__copy > * { animation: sl-hero-rise 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.8, 0.3, 1) both; }
  .sl-hero__copy > *:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.07s; }
  .sl-hero__copy > *:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.14s; }
  .sl-hero__copy > *:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: 0.21s; }
  .sl-hero__copy > *:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: 0.28s; }
  .sl-hero__copy > *:nth-child(6) { animation-delay: 0.35s; }
}
@keyframes sl-hero-rise {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(18px); }
}
@keyframes sl-hero-drift {
  from { transform: scale(1) translateX(0); }
  to { transform: scale(1.08) translateX(-1.5%); }
}
.sl-hero__inner {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 4;
  min-height: clamp(700px, 78svh, 860px);
  padding-top: clamp(96px, 11vw, 140px);
  padding-bottom: clamp(72px, 9vw, 120px);
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 0;
  align-items: end;
}
.sl-hero__copy {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 720px;
}
.sl-hero__signal-band {
  position: relative;
  z-index: 4;
  margin-top: 0;
  padding-top: clamp(8px, 1.5vw, 20px);
  padding-bottom: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px);
  display: flex;
  justify-content: flex-end;
}
.sl-hero__brand {
  margin: 0 0 16px;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 12px;
  color: var(--sl-bg-card);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-3xl);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  line-height: 1;
}
.sl-hero__brand span {
  width: 10px;
  height: 10px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--sl-accent);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 7px rgba(var(--sl-accent-rgb), 0.14);
  animation: sl-hero-pulse 2.4s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes sl-hero-pulse {
  0%, 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px rgba(var(--sl-accent-rgb), 0.1); }
  50% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 10px rgba(var(--sl-accent-rgb), 0.04); }
}
.sl-hero__title {
  max-width: 15ch;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-bg-card);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-4xl);
  font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.042em;
  line-height: 1.02;
  text-align: left;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.sl-hero__body {
  max-width: 40ch;
  margin: 18px 0 0;
  color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.78);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1.55;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  text-align: left;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.sl-hero__actions {
  margin: 28px 0 0;
  width: min(100%, 480px);
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
}
.sl-hero__primary,
.sl-hero__secondary {
  min-height: 52px;
  padding: 14px 22px;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-control);
}
.sl-hero__primary {
  border-color: var(--sl-accent);
  background: var(--sl-accent);
  color: var(--sl-night);
  box-shadow: 0 18px 38px -20px rgba(var(--sl-accent-rgb), 0.9);
}
.sl-hero__primary:hover {
  border-color: var(--sl-accent-hover);
  background: var(--sl-accent-hover);
  color: var(--sl-night);
}
.sl-hero__primary span:last-child { margin-left: 10px; transition: transform 0.2s ease; }
.sl-hero__primary:hover span:last-child { transform: translateX(4px); }
.sl-hero__secondary {
  border-color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.42);
  background: rgba(6, 17, 12, 0.36);
  color: var(--sl-bg);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
  backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
}
.sl-hero__secondary:hover {
  border-color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.8);
  background: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.1);
  color: #ffffff;
}
.sl-hero__primary:focus-visible,
.sl-hero__secondary:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid var(--sl-focus-dark);
  outline-offset: 4px;
}
.sl-hero__proof {
  width: fit-content;
  max-width: 100%;
  margin: 22px 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  justify-content: flex-start;
  gap: 8px 18px;
  list-style: none;
  border: 0;
  background: transparent;
}
.sl-hero__proof li {
  position: relative;
  padding-left: 14px;
  color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.62);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-hero__proof li::before {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  top: 0.42em;
  left: 0;
  width: 6px;
  height: 6px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: #75d59b;
}
.sl-hero__fine {
  margin: 14px 0 0;
  color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.58);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  text-align: left;
}
.sl-hero__signal {
  width: min(100%, 320px);
  margin: 0;
  padding: 18px 18px 16px;
  text-align: left;
  border: 1px solid rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.16);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius);
  background: rgba(5, 16, 10, 0.55);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
  backdrop-filter: blur(18px);
  box-shadow: 0 28px 64px -36px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);
}
.sl-hero__signal-head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 10px;
  color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.58);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sl-hero__signal-live { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; color: #8be4ad; }
.sl-hero__signal-live i {
  width: 7px;
  height: 7px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: currentColor;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px rgba(139, 228, 173, 0.12);
}
.sl-hero__trace {
  position: relative;
  height: 88px;
  margin-top: 14px;
  overflow: hidden;
  border: 1px solid rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.1);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
  background:
    linear-gradient(rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 1px, transparent 1px),
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03) 1px, transparent 1px),
    rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
  background-size: 24px 24px;
}
.sl-hero__trace-svg {
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
}
/* Defaults are the FULLY DRAWN still: reduced-motion, print, and any
   context without CSS animation all get a complete trace, never an empty
   grid. The keyframes below override these only while running. */
.sl-hero__trace-arc {
  fill: none;
  stroke: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.45);
  stroke-width: 1.6;
  stroke-linecap: round;
  stroke-dasharray: 100;
  stroke-dashoffset: 0;
}
.sl-hero__trace-strike {
  fill: none;
  stroke: #f28a32;
  stroke-width: 2.2;
  stroke-linecap: round;
  stroke-dasharray: 100;
  stroke-dashoffset: 0;
  filter: drop-shadow(0 0 7px rgba(242, 138, 50, 0.5));
}
.sl-hero__trace-tick path {
  fill: none;
  stroke: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.65);
  stroke-width: 1.2;
}
.sl-hero__trace-impact {
  fill: none;
  stroke: #f28a32;
  stroke-width: 1.4;
  opacity: 0;
  transform-box: fill-box;
  transform-origin: center;
}
.sl-hero__trace-ball {
  fill: var(--sl-bg);
  opacity: 0.9;
}
/* The 9.2s read cycle. Stops encode the engine's own benchmark: the
   backswing draws 3%→32% (2.67s), holds at the top, and the strike
   retraces 35.6%→45% (0.86s) — the 3:1 tempo_ratio target, animated.
   Then impact pulses, the read holds, fades, and the window rests. The
   77% jump-frames reset dash offsets while opacity is 0. */
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .sl-hero__trace-arc { animation: sl-swing-read 9.2s linear infinite; }
  .sl-hero__trace-strike { animation: sl-swing-strike 9.2s linear infinite; }
  .sl-hero__trace-tick--mid { animation: sl-swing-tick-mid 9.2s linear infinite; }
  .sl-hero__trace-tick--top { animation: sl-swing-tick-top 9.2s linear infinite; }
  .sl-hero__trace-impact { animation: sl-swing-impact 9.2s linear infinite; }
  .sl-hero__trace-ball { animation: sl-swing-anchor 9.2s linear infinite; }
  .sl-hero__signal-live i { animation: sl-live-blink 3.1s ease-in-out infinite; }
}
@keyframes sl-swing-read {
  0%, 2.9% { stroke-dashoffset: 100; opacity: 0; }
  3% { stroke-dashoffset: 100; opacity: 1; animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.33, 0, 0.45, 1); }
  32%, 69.9% { stroke-dashoffset: 0; opacity: 1; }
  76%, 76.9% { stroke-dashoffset: 0; opacity: 0; }
  77%, 100% { stroke-dashoffset: 100; opacity: 0; }
}
@keyframes sl-swing-strike {
  0%, 35.5% { stroke-dashoffset: -100; opacity: 0; }
  35.6% { stroke-dashoffset: -100; opacity: 1; animation-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0.55, 0, 0.85, 0.6); }
  45%, 69.9% { stroke-dashoffset: 0; opacity: 1; }
  76%, 76.9% { stroke-dashoffset: 0; opacity: 0; }
  77%, 100% { stroke-dashoffset: -100; opacity: 0; }
}
@keyframes sl-swing-tick-mid {
  0%, 17% { opacity: 0; }
  20%, 69.9% { opacity: 0.75; }
  76%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
}
@keyframes sl-swing-tick-top {
  0%, 31% { opacity: 0; }
  33%, 69.9% { opacity: 0.9; }
  76%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
}
@keyframes sl-swing-impact {
  0%, 44.9% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(0.25); }
  45% { opacity: 0.85; }
  53%, 100% { opacity: 0; transform: scale(1.15); }
}
@keyframes sl-swing-anchor {
  0%, 3% { opacity: 0; }
  8%, 69.9% { opacity: 0.9; }
  76%, 100% { opacity: 0; }
}
@keyframes sl-live-blink {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }
  50% { opacity: 0.35; }
}
.sl-hero__signal-grid {
  margin: 14px 0 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 0;
}
.sl-hero__signal-grid > div { min-width: 0; padding: 0 10px; }
.sl-hero__signal-grid > div:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
.sl-hero__signal-grid > div:last-child { padding-right: 0; }
.sl-hero__signal-grid > div + div { border-left: 1px solid rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.12); }
.sl-hero__signal-grid dt {
  color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.58);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-align: left;
}
.sl-hero__signal-grid dd {
  margin: 5px 0 0;
  color: var(--sl-bg);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 700;
  line-height: 1.3;
  text-align: left;
}
.sl-hero__signal-note {
  margin: 12px 0 0;
  color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.58);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  line-height: 1.4;
  text-align: left;
}
@media (max-width: 999px) {
  .sl-hero__title { font-size: var(--sl-text-4xl); }
}
@media (max-width: 749px) {
  .sl-hero {
    /* Roomy but not sprawling: the copy breathes and the compact signal
       card still lands within the first easy scroll. */
    --sl-mobile-hero-height: clamp(560px, calc(96svh - 180px), 660px);
    min-height: var(--sl-mobile-hero-height);
  }
  /* Bottom-anchored copy means the shade belongs at the BOTTOM. A modest
     band under the header keeps nav contrast, the middle opens up so the
     photograph actually shows, and the deep ramp starts where the type
     starts. The old gradient was 95% opaque at the top — a black field. */
  .sl-hero::before {
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.6) 0%, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.2) 26%, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.34) 52%, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.9) 100%),
      linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.28), rgba(4, 13, 9, 0.04));
  }
  .sl-hero::after {
    background-size: 48px 48px;
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000, transparent 68%);
    mask-image: linear-gradient(180deg, #000, transparent 68%);
  }
  .sl-hero__image { object-position: 32% center; }
  .sl-hero__inner {
    min-height: var(--sl-mobile-hero-height);
    padding-top: clamp(52px, 8vw, 68px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(40px, 7vw, 56px);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    align-content: end;
    justify-items: stretch;
    gap: 0;
  }
  /* The signal card stays on phones (the only visual showing what the
     product produces) — as a compact fact strip; rules further down. */
  .sl-hero__copy {
    margin-inline: 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .sl-hero__brand {
    font-size: var(--sl-text-2xl);
  }
  .sl-hero__title {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin-inline: 0;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-4xl);
    line-height: 1.02;
  }
  .sl-hero__body {
    max-width: 36ch;
    margin-inline: 0;
    margin-top: 16px;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
    line-height: 1.48;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .sl-hero__actions {
    width: min(100%, 320px);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
    margin: 24px 0 0;
  }
  .sl-hero__primary { width: 100%; min-height: 48px; padding: 12px 18px; }
  .sl-hero__secondary {
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 10px 16px;
    justify-self: stretch;
    justify-content: center;
    border: 1px solid rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.34);
    background: rgba(6, 17, 12, 0.42);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .sl-hero__secondary:hover { border-color: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.72); background: rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.1); }
  /* One quiet mono line: the 2-column grid orphaned the third chip and
     its green dots fought the orange brand dot. Middots, one color. */
  .sl-hero__proof {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: 4px 0;
  }
  .sl-hero__proof li {
    padding-left: 0;
    color: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.55);
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.09em;
  }
  .sl-hero__proof li::before { display: none; }
  .sl-hero__proof li + li::before {
    content: "\00B7";
    display: inline;
    position: static;
    margin: 0 var(--sl-space-2);
    background: none;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
  }
  .sl-hero__fine {
    max-width: 40ch;
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    color: rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.45);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .sl-hero__signal {
    width: 100%;
    padding: var(--sl-space-4) var(--sl-space-4) var(--sl-space-3);
  }
  /* The R2 pass hid the trace here because a static doodle didn't earn
     its rows. The live read does — it's the one moving proof of what the
     product produces — so it returns at a compact height above the
     fact-strip rows. */
  .sl-hero__trace { height: 64px; margin-top: 12px; }
  .sl-hero__signal-grid {
    margin-top: var(--sl-space-2);
    display: block;
  }
  .sl-hero__signal-grid > div {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--sl-space-3);
    padding: var(--sl-space-2) 0;
  }
  .sl-hero__signal-grid > div + div {
    border-left: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(238, 242, 239, 0.12);
  }
  .sl-hero__signal-grid dt { letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
  .sl-hero__signal-grid dd { margin: 0; text-align: right; }
  .sl-hero__signal-note { margin-top: var(--sl-space-2); }
  .sl-hero__signal-band {
    padding-top: var(--sl-space-3);
    padding-bottom: var(--sl-space-6);
  }
}
@media (max-width: 559px) {
  .sl-hero__brand { font-size: var(--sl-text-xl); letter-spacing: -0.03em; }
  .sl-hero__title { max-width: 10ch; font-size: var(--sl-text-4xl); }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .sl-hero__primary span { transition: none; }
  .sl-hero__brand span { animation: none; }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Premium hero",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Brand wordmark", "default": "CaddieInsight" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Bring one clear move to the range." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body", "default": "Choose the club, film one repeatable view, and get one prioritized coaching plan with a pass mark for your next clip." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "primary_label", "label": "Primary button label", "default": "Analyze a swing free" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "primary_url", "label": "Primary button link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "secondary_label", "label": "Secondary button label", "default": "Explore the sample report" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "secondary_url", "label": "Secondary button link" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "chip1", "label": "Proof point 1", "default": "1 REPORT / MONTH" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "chip2", "label": "Proof point 2", "default": "NO CARD" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "chip3", "label": "Proof point 3", "default": "CLUB SAVED" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "fine_print", "label": "Fine print", "default": "Supported 2D movement and timing estimates from phone video." },
    { "type": "video", "id": "video", "label": "Hero video (loops, muted)", "info": "A short 8–20s loop — filmed range or swing footage works best. No audio needed; it plays muted. Leave blank and the hero uses the photograph with a slow drift instead." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Desktop hero image", "info": "Fallback and poster when no video is set. Leave blank to use the packaged dusk-range artwork (caddieinsight-range-hero-desktop.webp)." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "mobile_image", "label": "Mobile hero image", "info": "Leave blank to use the packaged portrait companion (caddieinsight-range-hero-mobile.webp)." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "signal_club", "label": "Sample club", "default": "Iron" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "signal_priority", "label": "Sample priority", "default": "Lead-hip control" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "signal_target", "label": "Sample target", "default": "One pass mark" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Premium hero" }]
}
{% endschema %}
